  "title_original": "The Best 4K UHDs of 2026 & More: The Film Stage’s Holiday Gift Guide",
  "excerpt_original": "The holidays are upon us, so whether you’re looking for film-related gifts or simply want to get for yourself some of the finest this year has to offer, we have a gift guide for you. Including must-have books on filmmaking, the best from the Criterion Collection and other…",
  "published_at": "2026-11-18T14:33:04+00:00",
  "article_hash": "34e1e63a30920ab75af6d695b73cf074439b6297ae76543b3d9af7eab2c02bd7",
  "source_url": "https://thefilmstage.com/the-best-4k-uhds-of-2026-more-the-film-stage-holiday-gift-guide/",
  "article_status": "collected",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The holidays are upon us, so whether you’re looking for film-related gifts or simply want to get for yourself some of the finest this year has to offer, we have a gift guide for you. Including must-have books on filmmaking, the best from the Criterion Collection and other home-video lines, subscriptions, magazines, music, and more, dive in below."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The Best 4K UHDs & Blu-rays of 2026"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://thefilmstage.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/2026-10-26_Film-Stage_Kubrick-Criterion_A.-Sang-urai_IMG_1314-1200x800.jpg",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "credit": "The Film Stage"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "There’s no better gift than a proper film set, and the crown jewel this year is certainly the Criterion Collection’s The Complete Kubrick , for which we’ve dedicated a season-long celebration , including a wide-ranging interview with producer Michael Chaiken.",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "The Complete Kubrick",
          "url": "https://link.amazon/B0j4eyf0P"
        },
        {
          "text": "a season-long celebration",
          "url": "https://thefilmstage.com/the-complete-kubrick-a-season-of-celebrating-the-legendary-director/"
        },
        {
          "text": "a wide-ranging interview",
          "url": "https://thefilmstage.com/he-wanted-the-films-to-survive-michael-chaiken-on-assembling-the-complete-kubrick/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Additional box set highlights from Criterion this year include Martin Scorsese’s World Cinema Project No. 5 , Three Films by Leos Carax ( Boy Meets Girl / Mauvais sang / The Lovers on the Bridge ), I’ll Remind You of Everything: The Films of Mike Mills ( Beginners / 20th Century Women / C’mon C’mon ), and John Singleton’s Hood Trilogy ( Boyz n the Hood / Poetic Justice / Baby Boy ), as well as a trio of great new Eclipse line: The First Films of Samuel Fuller , Lubitsch Musicals , and Kinuyo Tanaka Directs .",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Martin Scorsese’s World Cinema Project No. 5",
          "url": "https://link.amazon/B06PQ7h8O"
        },
        {
          "text": "Three Films by Leos Carax",
          "url": "https://link.amazon/B0fnPQtM5"
        },
        {
          "text": "I’ll Remind You of Everything: The Films of Mike Mills",
          "url": "https://link.amazon/B020kSJ43"
        },
        {
          "text": "John Singleton’s Hood Trilogy",
          "url": "https://link.amazon/B04JtAeZ4"
        },
        {
          "text": "The First Films of Samuel Fuller",
          "url": "https://link.amazon/B04fOboug"
        },
        {
          "text": "Lubitsch Musicals",
          "url": "https://link.amazon/B0eXmApc1"
        },
        {
          "text": "Kinuyo Tanaka Directs",
          "url": "https://link.amazon/B08QtJ0Dw"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://thefilmstage.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Steven-Spielberg-1200x714.jpg",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "credit": "The Film Stage"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "To commemorate Matt Johnson’s major year, NEON has also delivered the must-own Nirvanna the Band the Show the Movie the Box Set , while Kino Lorber has Sergio Leone Masterworks and, high on the rewatchability factor, is Steven Spielberg: The Spotlight Collection .",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Nirvanna the Band the Show the Movie the Box Set",
          "url": "https://link.amazon/B02UrQ5we"
        },
        {
          "text": "Sergio Leone Masterworks",
          "url": "https://link.amazon/B005SBvWi"
        },
        {
          "text": "Steven Spielberg: The Spotlight Collection",
          "url": "https://link.amazon/B09AUa98w"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Check out our picks of the best individual-film releases throughout the year below."
