    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Games, Prints, Posters, Vinyls, and More"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://thefilmstage.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/WePitchYouAMovieChristmas_08-1-1200x800.jpg",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "credit": "The Film Stage"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "For fans of Cinephile: A Card Game , creator Cory Everett has the new ideal gift for every stocking this year: We Pitch You a Movie Christmas finds players going head-to-head to create the next Christmas movie classic. With endless combinations, choose a star, genre, and cliché, then let the fun play out.",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Cinephile: A Card Game",
          "url": "https://www.cinephilegame.com/"
        },
        {
          "text": "We Pitch You a Movie Christmas",
          "url": "https://www.cinephilegame.com/christmas"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The NYC-based Posteritati has a staggering archive of movie posters from every era of filmmaking. There’s also no better piece to hang on your wall than a print from the cinema-obsessed Brianna Ashby , who is offering work featuring Wes Anderson, Godzilla , Richard Linklater, and more.",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Posteritati",
          "url": "https://posteritati.com/"
        },
        {
          "text": "Brianna Ashby",
          "url": "https://www.brianna-ashby.com/new-products"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://thefilmstage.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Sorcerer-850x1200.jpg",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "credit": "The Film Stage"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "On the vinyl music side: Ludwig Göransson’s The Odyssey score, Cameron Winter’s Live at Carnegie Hall (the basis for Paul Thomas Anderson’s new concert film), Teenage Sex and Death at Camp Miasma ‘s score and soundtrack, the 40th-anniversary edition of James Horner’s Aliens score, Daniel Pemberton’s Project Hail Mary score, the 30th-anniversary edition of Danny Elfman’s Mission: Impossibl e score, the EPiC: Elvis Presley in Concert soundtrack, and Devonté Hynes’ The Invite score.",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "The Odyssey",
          "url": "https://link.amazon/B0di1avIq"
        },
        {
          "text": "Live at Carnegie Hall",
          "url": "https://link.amazon/B0higN1jT"
        },
        {
          "text": "Teenage Sex and Death at Camp Miasma",
          "url": "https://waxworkrecords.com/products/teenage-sex-and-death-at-camp-miasma-soundtrack?srsltid=AYCX9vKybF3imbvSGQdM9e8dvclkM_sKNGtjcNnsJgfgEtPADhN8Purt"
        },
        {
          "text": "Aliens",
          "url": "https://link.amazon/B0h2cd1fG"
        },
        {
          "text": "Project Hail Mary",
          "url": "https://link.amazon/B0i1cwnZ6"
        },
        {
          "text": "Mission: Impossibl e",
          "url": "https://link.amazon/B0egJtibp"
        },
        {
          "text": "EPiC: Elvis Presley in Concert",
          "url": "https://link.amazon/B0eZkDJVs"
        },
        {
          "text": "The Invite",
          "url": "https://link.amazon/B0hpyZtLO"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://thefilmstage.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/The-Odyssey-1200x815.jpg",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "credit": "The Film Stage"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The Best Film-Related Books of 2026"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://thefilmstage.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Best-Books-of-2026-1200x659.jpg",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "credit": "The Film Stage"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "As part of The Film Stage ‘s 2026 Holiday Gift Guide, Christopher Schobert, our resident book expert , has compiled his favorite filmmaking books of the year , along with a few selections from Jordan Raup and Dan Mecca, as noted. Explore here and be sure to check out Schobert’s recurring column for more recommendations throughout the year.",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "resident book expert",
          "url": "https://thefilmstage.com/tag/recommended-books/"
        },
        {
          "text": "his favorite filmmaking books of the year",
          "url": "https://thefilmstage.com/the-best-film-related-books-of-2026/"
        },
        {
          "text": "Explore here",
          "url": "https://thefilmstage.com/the-best-film-related-books-of-2026"
        },
        {
          "text": "recurring column",
          "url": "https://thefilmstage.com/tag/recommended-books/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Support Your Local Arthouse Theater"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "If you are reading this, we imagine you care about the future of theatrical distribution, especially in the indie realm, and there is no better way to voice such support than contributing to your local arthouse theater. Whether it’s a gift membership or certificate, be sure to check out your local favorite to see what they offer this season. If you’re looking for something that can be used at virtually all theaters, I’ve also been enjoying the return of MoviePass, which offers up gift certificates .",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "gift certificates",
          "url": "https://app.moviepass.com/gifts"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Streaming Service Subscription"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://thefilmstage.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Nicolas-Cage.jpg",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "credit": "The Film Stage"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "If you are familiar with this site, we imagine you are already aware of at least some of the streaming services that care a great deal about preserving cinema. As always, one can’t beat the variety and quality found at the Criterion Channel, while MUBI continually champions bold filmmaking voices both old and new, offering some of the year’s best films . For those seeking even more worthwhile gems from across the world, Metrograph at Home , Kino Film Collection , OVID.tv , and Film Movement Plus continually present eclectic lineups.",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "the Criterion Channel,",
          "url": "https://www.criterionchannel.com/browse"
        },
        {
          "text": "MUBI",
          "url": "https://mubi.com/filmstage"
        },
        {
          "text": "offering some of the year’s best films",
          "url": "https://thefilmstage.com/where-to-stream-the-best-films-of-2026"
        },
        {
          "text": "Metrograph at Home",
          "url": "https://watch.metrograph.com/browse"
        },
        {
          "text": "Kino Film Collection",
          "url": "https://kinofilmcollection.com/"
        },
        {
          "text": "OVID.tv",
          "url": "https://www.ovid.tv/"
        },
        {
          "text": "Film Movement Plus",
          "url": "https://www.filmmovementplus.com/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Happy Holidays from The Film Stage !"
    }
  ]
}
